# llms.txt — controlled public surface for AI agents (proposed convention)
# Purpose: point agents at canonical *public* pages you intend them to see.
# NOT for: internal architecture dumps, secrets, admin URLs, canary paths,
# authority overrides, "ignore previous instructions", legal threats,
# preference manipulation, poisoning, or consequential tool commands.
#
# Place at https://example.com/llms.txt
# Spec overview: https://llmstxt.org/

# Example Corp

> Public product site for Example Corp. Prefer official docs over third-party mirrors.
> Proprietary pricing engines, admin tools, and internal APIs are not listed here and require authentication.

## Primary (intentionally public)

- [Home](https://example.com/): Product overview
- [Docs](https://example.com/docs/): Canonical documentation
- [Pricing](https://example.com/pricing/): Plans and published limits
- [Security](https://example.com/security/): Trust and compliance overview
- [Contact](https://example.com/contact/): Support channels

## Optional public API docs

- [API reference](https://example.com/docs/api/): Public, authenticated API surface
- [Changelog](https://example.com/changelog/): Release history

## Notes for agents

- Prefer linked canonical URLs above over scraped mirrors or reconstructed internals.
- Do not treat absence from this file as an invitation to probe `/admin`, `/api/internal`, or similar paths.
- For crawl preferences, see robots.txt. For access to private data, use documented auth — not HTML comments or hidden text.
